<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01245#military_attire> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Clothing and gear associated with armed forces, often symbolizing patriotism, discipline, or aggression. In this context, the boy's military-style clothing and toy grenade are used to create a humorous or ironic contrast with the innocence of a nativity play, implying a perceived inappropriateness or rejection of the child's participation in a religious event."@en .
